From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:54:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] greeter: keep the text cursor inside the input field

The cursor is drawn from y - ascent down to y - ascent + height, with
height the text font's ascent + descent, while the input field's interior
ends PROMPT_H (5/4 of the line height, rounded down) below its top.  With
a font whose descent is a larger share of its height, such as DejaVu Sans
through Xft, the cursor's foot landed on the field's lower frame line, and
erasing the cursor (with the field's colour) cut gaps into the frame, one
per character typed.  The cursor's height is limited to the interior.
---
 greeter/Login.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/greeter/Login.c b/greeter/Login.c
index 8d46f5d..408c26f 100644
--- a/greeter/Login.c
+++ b/greeter/Login.c
@@ -474,6 +474,13 @@ realizeCursor (LoginWidget w, GC gc)
     y = PROMPT_Y (w, w->login.activePrompt);
     height = (F_ASCENT(text) + F_DESCENT(text));
     width = 1;
+    /* the I-beam (its foot is drawn at y - ascent + height) stays inside the
+       input field, whose interior ends at y + PROMPT_H - ascent - descent -
+       inframeswidth: with a font whose descent is a larger share of its
+       height (DejaVu Sans through Xft) the foot was on the field's frame, and
+       erasing the cursor left gaps in the frame */
+    if (height > PROMPT_H(w) - F_DESCENT(text) - w->login.inframeswidth)
+	height = PROMPT_H(w) - F_DESCENT(text) - w->login.inframeswidth;
 
     switch (PROMPT_STATE(w, w->login.activePrompt)) {
     case LOGIN_PROMPT_NOT_SHOWN:
